Observations/Interviews
- Observation
	- when interacting with the game, users find it fun to simply zoom around the screen with the player, which shows that smooth movement  is an important factor to gameplay
	- the game is easy to understand, shoot enemies while dodging their laser
	- game gets harder as time goes on, once you get ten points a new more difficult enemy type spawns
	- new mechanics are introduced as time goes on (enemies shooting multiple lasers)
- Interviews
	- What are you looking for from a game
		- Low level of entry, continuous engagement throughout playing
	- When would you use the game?
		- In class
		- Busy work
		- Game serves as an outlet/break from other more serious tasks, it should be distracting but not too distracting (easy to start and easy to end)
Personas
- Highschool student stuck in online class during covid. School has become so boring from home, not being able to interact with friends while still needing to attend classes. An outlet like a simple bullet-hell can be a fun break from class
- Gamer who is obsessed with beating their last score, always pushing to prove that they can do better than they did last time
